cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Work that uses CelloType should cite the thesis below, and the segmentation
  models behind its results (Cellpose-SAM, Cellpose, and StarDist when used),
  as listed in the README.
title: CelloType
abstract: >-
  Local web application for the segmentation and quantification of
  multichannel fluorescence microscopy images: dataset organisation,
  Cellpose-SAM segmentation (or StarDist for nuclei), mask review, per-object
  measurement on every channel and descriptive analysis in one guided
  workflow.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Herrlein
    given-names: Abril
    affiliation: Instituto Tecnológico de Buenos Aires (ITBA)
repository-code: "https://github.com/abrilcode/CelloType"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - fluorescence microscopy
  - image analysis
  - cell segmentation
  - nuclei segmentation
  - Cellpose
  - StarDist
  - bioimage analysis
preferred-citation:
  type: thesis
  title: >-
    Desarrollo de una plataforma web para segmentación y cuantificación de
    imágenes de fluorescencia multicanal
  authors:
    - family-names: Herrlein
      given-names: Abril
  thesis-type: "Proyecto final de carrera, Bioingeniería"
  institution:
    name: Instituto Tecnológico de Buenos Aires
  year: 2026
  url: "https://github.com/abrilcode/CelloType"
